      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Camden and Atlantic Railroad arrived in 1854, sparking Voorhees’ growth and later becoming the Pennsylvania‑Reading Seashore Line with three stations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.southjersey.com/articles/?articleID=13451",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlers were the Lenni‑Lenape, the original Algonquian people who inhabited the area long before European arrival.",
